dressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>HANAWA TAKAYUKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>IMAIZUMI KATSUICHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KOMATSU YASUO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NAKAMURA KAZUNARI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TAKEHANA SAKAE</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>DOGUCHI, NOBUYUKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HANAWA, TAKAYUKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>IMAIZUMI, KATSUICHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KOMATSU, YASUO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NAKAMURA, KAZUNARI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAKEHANA, SAKAE</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>An endoscope (2) includes a head (6), the front end of which encloses a variable-sensitivity CCD (9) capable of changing its sensitivity responsive to a plurality of pulsated drive signals. The endoscope (2) is connected detachably with a processor (3) so that a ROM (48) storing information such as the type of the endoscope can supply such information to control means (21) in the processor (3). The control means (21) determines the sensitivity of the CCD (9) by sensitivity control means (12) depending on the connected endoscope (2), thus allowing appropriately bright images to be observed independently of the type of endoscope (2) in use.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un endoscope (2) muni d'une tête (6) dont l'extrémité avant renferme un dispositif DTC à sensibilité variable (9), lequel est capable de modifier sa sensibilité en réponse à une pluralité de signaux d'attaque pulsés. Cet endoscope (2) est raccordé de manière détachable à un processeur (3), de sorte qu'une mémoire morte (48) destinée à stocker des informations, concernant par exemple le type d'endoscope utilisé, peut fournir ces informations à des moyens de commande (21) placés à l'intérieur dudit processeur (3). Ces moyens de commande (21) sont conçus pour déterminer la sensibilité du dispositif DTC (9) à l'aide de moyens d'évaluation de la sensibilité (12), en fonction de l'endoscope (2). On peut ainsi observer des images suffisamment nettes, quel que soit le type d'endoscope (2) utilisé.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>